        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Bulk Plan ID Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775315954757"
          },
          "code": "BULK_PLAN_ID_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1775199409555",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775199409557_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Bulk Plan ID extractor for an Oracle Transportation Management (OTM) Diagnostic Assistant.\n\nYour task is to:\n1. Extract a valid Bulk Plan ID from the user query.\n2. Handle follow-up context using previously resolved Bulk Plan ID.\n\n# ============================================================\n# INPUT\n# ============================================================\nUser Query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\npreviousBulkPlanId: {{$context.$variables.bulkPlanId}}\n\n# ============================================================\n# VALID BULK PLAN ID RULES\n# ============================================================\nA valid Bulk Plan ID MUST satisfy ALL of the following:\n\n1. Structure must be:\n   <DOMAIN>.<XID>\n\n2. DOMAIN:\n   - Appears before the dot (.)\n   - Must be non-empty\n   - Can contain letters, numbers, underscore\n\n3. XID:\n   - Appears after the dot (.)\n   - Must match the following regex:\n     ^([^\\,x><=/&\\?;#\\$\\'\\\"\\r\\n\\)\\(\\.]+?)$\n\n   - This means:\n     - Must NOT contain: , x > < = / & ? ; # $ ' \" ( ) .\n     - Must NOT contain newline characters\n     - Must NOT be empty\n\n4. The ID must look like a system-generated OTM identifier, NOT a natural language phrase.\n\nExamples of VALID Bulk Plan IDs:\n- GLOGOWNER.BULKPLAN_12345\n- ABCD.PLAN_20240101\n- TESTDOMAIN.XYZ_001\n\nExamples of INVALID values:\n- BULKPLAN (no domain)\n- DOMAIN.HELLO WORLD (contains space)\n- DOMAIN.XID.TEST (multiple dots)\n- DOMAIN.XID?<123 (invalid character)\n\n# ============================================================\n# EXTRACTION RULES\n# ============================================================\n1. Scan the entire query for tokens matching:\n   <DOMAIN>.<XID>\n2. Extract exactly ONE valid Bulk Plan ID.\n3. If multiple candidates exist:\n   → Choose the most valid system-generated identifier.\n4. Normalize the result to UPPERCASE.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nFOLLOW-UP CONTEXT RULE (STRICT PRIORITY)\n------------------------------------------------------------\nResolve Bulk Plan ID using the following order:\n1. If a valid Bulk Plan ID is found in the current query:\n   → Use it\n\n2. Else if previousBulkPlanId exists:\n   → Use previousBulkPlanId\n\n3. Else:\n   → bulkPlanId = null\n\n# ============================================================\n# OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON)\n# ============================================================\n\n{\n  \"bulkPlanId\": \"<BULK_PLAN_ID or null>\",\n  \"extractionLogic\": \"short extraction logic\"\n}\n\nDo not include any additional fields.\nDo not include explanations.\nReturn only valid JSON."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"extractionLogic\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"bulkPlanId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Diagnostic Log ID Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775315954757"
          },
          "code": "DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775207870412",
          "id": "1768293343616",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768293343617_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Diagnostic Log ID Resolver for an Oracle Transportation Management (OTM) Bulk Plan Diagnostic Assistant.\n\nYour responsibilities:\n1. Extract a Diagnostic Log File ID from the user query.\n2. Derive the Bulk Plan ID from it.\n3. Handle follow-up context using previously resolved identifiers.\n\n============================================================\nINPUT\n============================================================\nUser Query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\npreviousDiagnosticLogFileId: {{$context.$variables.diagnosticLogFileId}}\npreviousBulkPlanId: {{$context.$variables.bulkPlanId}}\n\n============================================================\nSTEP A — DIAGNOSTIC LOG ID EXTRACTION\n============================================================\nIdentify a token in the user query that resembles an OTM Diagnostic Log File ID.\n\nStructure: <DOMAIN>.<XID>_<LOG_PROCESS_ID>\n\nFIELD DEFINITIONS:\nDOMAIN\n• identifier representing the OTM domain\n\nXID\n• appears after the dot (.)\n• MUST match the following regex:\n  ^([^\\,x><=/&\\?;#\\$\\'\\\"\\r\\n\\)\\(\\.]+?)$\n\n• This means:\n  - Must NOT contain: , x > < = / & ? ; # $ ' \" ( ) .\n  - Must NOT contain newline characters\n  - Must NOT be empty\n\nLOG_PROCESS_ID\n• numeric process execution identifier after underscore (_)\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPATTERN DEFINITION\n------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Diagnostic Log File ID follows this exact structure: <DOMAIN>.<XID>_<LOG_PROCESS_ID>\nWhere:\n- DOMAIN: alphanumeric identifier before the dot (.)\n- XID: must satisfy the strict validation rules defined above\n- LOG_PROCESS_ID: numeric identifier after the underscore (_)\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nPATTERN CHARACTERISTICS\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- Exactly ONE dot (.) separating DOMAIN and XID\n- Exactly ONE underscore (_) separating XID and LOG_PROCESS_ID\n- LOG_PROCESS_ID must be numeric\n- XID MUST strictly follow the defined regex constraint\n- XID must NOT be empty\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nREFERENCE PATTERN (GUIDANCE ONLY)\n------------------------------------------------------------\n[A-Za-z0-9]+\\.<XID>_[0-9]+\n\nNote:\n- The exact validity of XID is governed ONLY by the regex rule defined earlier\n- Do NOT rely on this pattern alone for validation\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nVALID EXAMPLES\n------------------------------------------------------------\nRITO.20260303-0001_247523  \nGLOGOWNER.BULKPLAN_001  \nABC.20250101-0001_12345  \n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nEXTRACTION RULES\n------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Scan the entire query for tokens matching:\n   <DOMAIN>.<XID>_<NUMBER>\n\n2. The token may appear anywhere in the sentence.\n3. Prefer tokens containing BOTH:\n   • a dot (.)\n   • an underscore (_)\n\n4. STRICT VALIDATION:\n   - Extract ONLY if XID satisfies the regex constraint above\n   - If XID violates the rule, IGNORE that candidate\n\n5. Extract exactly ONE valid ID.\n6. Normalize the extracted ID to UPPERCASE.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nFOLLOW-UP CONTEXT RULE (STRICT PRIORITY)\n------------------------------------------------------------\nResolve Diagnostic Log File ID using the following order:\n\n1. If a valid Diagnostic Log File ID is found in the current query:\n   → Use it\n\n2. Else if previousDiagnosticLogFileId exists:\n   → Use previousDiagnosticLogFileId\n\n3. Else:\n   → diagnosticLogFileId = null\n\n============================================================\nSTEP B — BULK PLAN ID DERIVATION\n============================================================\nResolve Bulk Plan ID using the following order:\n\n1. If diagnosticLogFileId is resolved:\n   → Bulk Plan ID = substring before the LAST underscore (_)\n\n   Example:\n   RITO.20260303-0001_247523\n   → RITO.20260303-0001\n\n2. Else if a Bulk Plan ID is explicitly present in the query:\n   → Extract it if it matches <DOMAIN>.<XID>\n\n3. Else if previousBulkPlanId exists:\n   → Use previousBulkPlanId\n\n4. Else:\n   → bulkPlanId = null\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nDERIVATION RULES\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- Diagnostic Log ID format: <BULK_PLAN_GID>_<LOG_PROCESS_ID>\n- Bulk Plan ID = portion before the LAST underscore (_)\n- Bulk Plan ID must be in the form: <DOMAIN>.<XID>\n- Preserve values exactly after uppercasing\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON)\n============================================================\nRespond ONLY with valid JSON in the following format:\n\n{\n  \"diagnosticLogFileId\": \"<LOGFILE_ID or null>\",\n  \"bulkPlanId\": \"<DOMAIN_NAME.XID or null>\",\n  \"diagnosticLogFileIdExtractionLogic\": \"One short sentence describing the extraction logic for diagnosticLogFileId\"\n}\n\nDo not include any additional fields.\nDo not include explanations.\nReturn only valid JSON."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"diagnosticLogFileId\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"bulkPlanId\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n    \"diagnosticLogFileIdExtractionLogic\": {\n      \"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]\n    },\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"diagnosticLogFileId\", \"bulkPlanId\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Merge Identifiers",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const inputIdType = ($context.$variables && $context.$variables.inputIdType) || \"DIAG_LOG_FILE_GID\";\nconst diagExtractorNode = ($context.$nodes.DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR && $context.$nodes.DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR.$output) || {};\nconst bulkExtractorNode = ($context.$nodes.BULK_PLAN_ID_EXTRACTOR && $context.$nodes.BULK_PLAN_ID_EXTRACTOR.$output) || {};\nconst fetchNode = ($context.$nodes.FETCH_BULK_PLAN_DATA && $context.$nodes.FETCH_BULK_PLAN_DATA.$output) || {};\n\nconst existingBulkPlanId = ($context.$variables.bulkPlanId) || null;\nconst existingDiagnosticLogFileId = ($context.$variables.diagnosticLogFileId) || null;\n\nlet diagnosticLogFileId = null;\nlet bulkPlanId = null;\nif (inputIdType === \"DIAG_LOG_FILE_GID\") {\n    if (diagExtractorNode.diagnosticLogFileId && typeof diagExtractorNode.diagnosticLogFileId === \"string\") {\n        diagnosticLogFileId = diagExtractorNode.diagnosticLogFileId.trim().toUpperCase();\n        if (diagnosticLogFileId.includes(\"_\")) {\n            const idx = diagnosticLogFileId.lastIndexOf(\"_\");\n            if (idx > 0) {\n                bulkPlanId = diagnosticLogFileId.substring(0, idx);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Fallback to existing if extractor fails\n    if (!diagnosticLogFileId) {\n        diagnosticLogFileId = existingDiagnosticLogFileId;\n        bulkPlanId = existingBulkPlanId;\n    }\n} else if (inputIdType === \"BULK_PLAN_GID\") {\n    if (bulkExtractorNode.bulkPlanId && typeof bulkExtractorNode.bulkPlanId === \"string\") {\n        bulkPlanId = bulkExtractorNode.bulkPlanId.trim().toUpperCase();\n    }\n    if (bulkPlanId && fetchNode.logProcessId !== undefined && fetchNode.logProcessId !== null) {\n        const processId = String(fetchNode.logProcessId).trim();\n        if (processId) {\n            diagnosticLogFileId = bulkPlanId + \"_\" + processId;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (!diagnosticLogFileId) {\n        diagnosticLogFileId = existingDiagnosticLogFileId;\n    }\n    if (!bulkPlanId) {\n        bulkPlanId = existingBulkPlanId;\n    }\n}\nvar result = {\n    diagnosticLogFileId: diagnosticLogFileId || null,\n    bulkPlanId: bulkPlanId || null\n};\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775211111104"
          },
          "code": "MERGE_IDENTIFIERS",
          "id": "1775208955362",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Domain Scope Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772556852321"
          },
          "code": "DOMAIN_SCOPE_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1775211111104",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775211111105_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Domain Scope Classifier for an Oracle Transportation Management (OTM) Bulk Plan Diagnostic Assistant.\n\nYour task is to determine whether the user query is related to OTM Bulk Plan execution and planning diagnostics.\n\n============================================================\nINPUT\n============================================================\nUser Query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChat History: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n============================================================\nSCOPE DEFINITION\n============================================================\nThe assistant supports ONLY the Oracle Transportation Management (OTM) Bulk Plan execution domain.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nIN SCOPE\n------------------------------------------------------------\nA query is IN SCOPE if it relates to OTM Bulk Plan execution, planning, diagnostics, or follow-up interaction on previously established OTM Bulk Plan results, including:\n- bulk plan runs\n- diagnostic logs\n- orders, shipments, routing\n- rate evaluation, rating engine\n- service provider selection\n- multistop consolidation\n- equipment, lanes, locations\n- planning workflow steps\n- execution failures or root causes\n- shipment creation or planning results\n- follow-up questions about previously shown OTM results\n- requests to reformat, summarize, restate, or display previously shown OTM results differently\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nOUT OF SCOPE\n------------------------------------------------------------\nA query is OUT OF SCOPE if it:\n- is unrelated to OTM Bulk Plan execution\n- asks about general knowledge or other domains\n- involves coding, programming, math, weather, translation, or personal questions\n- is conversational and not related to OTM planning, diagnostics, or previously established OTM results\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nFOLLOW-UP CONTINUITY RULE (MANDATORY)\n------------------------------------------------------------\nIf the current query is a follow-up to previously established OTM Bulk Plan analysis in chatHistory, then it remains IN SCOPE when it asks to:\n- reformat prior results\n- display prior results differently\n- summarize prior results\n- simplify prior results\n- show the same data in table, list, bullet, or HTML format\n- explain a previously shown result in more detail\n\nExamples of IN SCOPE follow-ups:\n- show this in a table\n- show this data in HTML table format\n- summarize this\n- explain this result\n- show the failed orders only\n- display the multistop savings as a list\n\nIn these cases:\n- Do NOT evaluate the query independently from prior context\n- Do NOT require the user to restate the Bulk Plan ID or Diagnostic Log File ID\n- Treat the query as IN SCOPE if the referenced prior result was in scope\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\nIMPORTANT RULES\n------------------------------------------------------------\n- DO NOT use identifiers alone (Bulk Plan ID or Diagnostic Log ID) to determine scope\n- Presence of IDs does NOT automatically make a query in scope\n- Use chatHistory to determine whether the query is a follow-up to previously established OTM Bulk Plan analysis\n- If the query changes only presentation or formatting of prior OTM results, it is still IN SCOPE\n- Focus on whether the query is about OTM planning, diagnostics, or previously established OTM diagnostic results\n\n============================================================\nDECISION RULE\n============================================================\nIf ANY of the following are true:\n1. The query clearly relates to OTM Bulk Plan execution or planning\n2. The query is a follow-up to previously established in-scope OTM Bulk Plan analysis\n3. The query asks to reformat or restate previously shown OTM Bulk Plan results\nThen:\n    isOutOfScope = false\n\nOtherwise:\n    isOutOfScope = true\n\n============================================================\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON)\n============================================================\n\n{\n  \"isOutOfScope\": true | false,\n  \"scopeReason\": \"<one short sentence explaining why the query is in or out of scope>\"\n}\n\nDo not include any additional fields.\nDo not include explanations outside the JSON.\nReturn only valid JSON."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"scopeReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"isOutOfScope\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Resolve Input Type",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let rawInputType = null;\nif ($context.$system.$inputContext && typeof $context.$system.$inputContext.inputType === \"string\") {\n    rawInputType = $context.$system.$inputContext.inputType.trim().toUpperCase();\n}\n\nlet resolvedInputType = \"DIAG_LOG_FILE_GID\"; // default\nif (rawInputType === \"BULK PLAN\") {\n    resolvedInputType = \"BULK_PLAN_GID\";\n} else if (rawInputType === \"DIAGNOSTICS\") {\n    resolvedInputType = \"DIAG_LOG_FILE_GID\";\n}\n\nreturn resolvedInputType;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775199228184"
          },
          "code": "RESOLVE_INPUT_TYPE",
          "id": "1775398476519",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Resolve Bulk Plan Fetch",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const inputIdType = $context.$variables.inputIdType || \"DIAG_LOG_FILE_GID\";\nconst bulkExtractorNode = ($context.$nodes.BULK_PLAN_ID_EXTRACTOR && $context.$nodes.BULK_PLAN_ID_EXTRACTOR.$output) || {};\nconst diagExtractorNode = ($context.$nodes.DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR && $context.$nodes.DIAGNOSTIC_LOG_ID_EXTRACTOR.$output) || {};\n\nconst existingBulkPlanId = $context.$variables.bulkPlanId || null;\nconst existingSummary = $context.$variables.bulkPlanExecutionSummary || null;\nlet candidateBulkPlanId = null;\n\nif (inputIdType === \"BULK_PLAN_GID\") {\n    candidateBulkPlanId = (bulkExtractorNode.bulkPlanId && String(bulkExtractorNode.bulkPlanId).trim().toUpperCase()) || null;\n} else if (inputIdType === \"DIAG_LOG_FILE_GID\") {\n    candidateBulkPlanId = (diagExtractorNode.bulkPlanId && String(diagExtractorNode.bulkPlanId).trim().toUpperCase()) || null;\n}\n\nif (!candidateBulkPlanId) {\n    candidateBulkPlanId = existingBulkPlanId;\n}\n\nlet shouldFetch = false;\nif (candidateBulkPlanId) {\n    if (!existingSummary) {\n        shouldFetch = true;\n    } else if (!existingBulkPlanId) {\n        shouldFetch = true;\n    } else if (candidateBulkPlanId !== existingBulkPlanId) {\n        shouldFetch = true;\n    }\n}\n\nvar result = {\n    shouldFetch: shouldFetch,\n    bulkPlanId: candidateBulkPlanId,\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775313928756"
          },
          "code": "RESOLVE_BULK_PLAN_FETCH",
